-- title:
--   Simple-root place criterion along a finite morphism
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $F$, $F'$ be fields, with $F$ and $F'$ algebras over $K$, $F$ of characteristic zero, and assume $F'$ has principal divisors over $K$, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F'$ admits a divisor $D$ on the places of $F'$ over $K$ with $D(v) = \operatorname{ord}_v f$ for all $v$ and $\deg D = 0$. Let $\varphi : F \to F'$ be a $K$-algebra map which is integral as a ring homomorphism and along which $F'$ is a finite $F$-module. Let $v$ be a place of $K$-type on $F$, i.e. a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}_v \subsetneq F$ containing $\varphi$-independently the image of $K$ and which is a principal ideal ring, and let $Q \in \mathcal{O}_v[Y]$ be monic. Suppose $x \in F'$ satisfies $(\varphi Q)(x) = 0$, where $Q$ is first mapped into $F[Y]$ and then evaluated through $\varphi$, and let $b \in \mathcal{O}_v$ satisfy: $\operatorname{ord}_v(Q(b)) > 0$, the element $Q'(b)$ is a unit of $\mathcal{O}_v$, and $\operatorname{ord}_v \bigl(N_{F'/F}(x - \varphi(b))\bigr) = \operatorname{ord}_v(Q(b))$, the norm being taken for the $F$-algebra structure on $F'$ given by $\varphi$. Then there is a place $w_0$ of $F'$ whose valuation subring pulls back along $\varphi$ to $\mathcal{O}_v$, with $\operatorname{ord}_{w_0}(x - \varphi(b)) > 0$, with ramification index $1$ along $\varphi$ (the least $n > 0$ of the form $\operatorname{ord}_{w_0}(\varphi f)$, $f \in F^\times$, equals $1$) and residue degree $1$ along $\varphi$, and $w_0$ is the only place of $F'$ restricting to $v$ along $\varphi$ at which $x - \varphi(b)$ has positive order.
--
--   This is a place-theoretic form of Hensel's lemma, or of Kummer's theorem on the decomposition of a place in an extension generated by a root of a polynomial with a simple reduction, with the usual approximation input replaced by the hypothesis on the order of the norm of $x - \varphi(b)$. It is used in the analysis of places on modular curves under degeneracy maps, where $Q$ is a modular polynomial and $b$ a lift of a residue root, both in the level-one and in the level-$N$ specialisation arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_place_over_of_simple_root_along.lean

